2026-10-20|Sum of All Sortable Integers

Question:
Given an integer array nums of length n, find the sum of all positive integers k such that:
- k divides n.
- Partitioning nums into consecutive subarrays of length k allows each subarray to be cyclically rotated independently so that the entire array becomes sorted in non-decreasing order.

Approach:
1. Create a sorted copy of nums. This represents the array we want to obtain.
2. Find all divisors k of n, because only divisors can divide the array into equal-sized blocks.
3. For each candidate k, examine every consecutive block of length k.
4. Check whether each block can be transformed into its corresponding sorted block using a cyclic rotation.
5. A block can be transformed into its target block if some cyclic shift makes every element match the target block at the same positions.
6. If every block passes this check, add k to the answer.
7. Return the sum of all valid k values.

Solution:

class Solution {
private:
    bool canRotateToTarget(const vector<int>& nums,
                           const vector<int>& sorted,
                           int start, int k) {
        // Build the KMP prefix array for the sorted block.
        vector<int> lps(k, 0);

        for (int i = 1, len = 0; i < k; ) {
            if (sorted[start + i] == sorted[start + len]) {
                lps[i++] = ++len;
            } else if (len > 0) {
                len = lps[len - 1];
            } else {
                lps[i++] = 0;
            }
        }

        // Search for the sorted block in the cyclic nums block.
        // A cycle of length k needs at most 2*k - 1 elements.
        int matched = 0;

        for (int j = 0; j < 2 * k - 1; j++) {
            int value = nums[start + (j % k)];

            while (matched > 0 &&
                   value != sorted[start + matched]) {
                matched = lps[matched - 1];
            }

            if (value == sorted[start + matched]) {
                matched++;
            }

            if (matched == k) {
                return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }

public:
    long long sortableIntegers(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();

        vector<int> sorted = nums;
        sort(sorted.begin(), sorted.end());

        long long answer = 0;

        for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {
            if (n % k != 0) {
                continue;
            }

            bool valid = true;

            for (int start = 0; start < n; start += k) {
                if (!canRotateToTarget(nums, sorted, start, k)) {
                    valid = false;
                    break;
                }
            }

            if (valid) {
                answer += k;
            }
        }

        return answer;
    }
};


Time Complexity: O(n log n + n × sum of k² over all divisors k of n) in the worst case for this direct approach, including sorting and checking cyclic shifts.

Space Complexity: O(n) for the sorted copy.
